title: Route asset owner changes through one setter and let PSM admins follow the owner
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `pallet-assets` gains `AssetsCallback::owner_changed` with a default no-op body. All
    three owner mutations (`transfer_ownership`, `force_asset_status`, `reset_team`) now go
    through one internal setter that fires the callback.

    `pallet-psm` gains `handle_internal_asset_owner_change` for runtimes to wire into that
    callback. A PSM admin role that equals the departing owner's signed origin follows the
    ownership; any other admin origin does not change. This removes the silent split where
    an asset transfer left the previous owner holding the PSM admin role.
crates:
- name: pallet-assets
  bump: minor
- name: pallet-psm
  bump: minor
